      "notes": "[Call Note · 09 Sept 2026 04:29 pm · Connected (3 min)]: OSPER FORMULATIONS\n\n91 9958786797 | osperbaddi@gmail.com | Baddi | Dry powder injection specialist\n\nThis is the most technically specialized lead in this batch. Osper has a dedicated dry-powder injection facility, with public exhibition information stating an installed capacity of one lakh vials per shift; CDSCO's current WHO-GMP/CoPP data also lists Osper for sterile dry powder injections, including general and beta-lactam categories.\n\nAI OPPORTUNITIES\n\n1. RFQ → DRY-INJECTION MANUFACTURING FIT\n\nPain Point: A dry-powder injectable enquiry needs to be checked against product category, sterile capability, beta-lactam/general classification and manufacturing feasibility.\nSaivyy: Read RFQ/specification → identify the matching Osper capability and flag technical gaps.\nHelps: Reduces time spent manually qualifying enquiries.\nAsk: “When you receive a new dry-powder injectable RFQ, how much manual checking is involved before your team knows whether Osper can manufacture it?”\n\n2. BATCH HISTORY → PRODUCT-SPECIFIC RISK\n\nPain Point: For sterile dry powders, recurring deviations may be hidden across years of batch records.\nSaivyy: Connect batch parameters, environmental data, QC results and deviation history → identify repeat patterns by product.\nHelps: Earlier detection of quality risk.\n\n3. BETA-LACTAM vs GENERAL → SEPARATE INTELLIGENCE\n\nPain Point: Osper handles both general and beta-lactam sterile dry powders.\nSaivyy: Create separate risk/production analytics for each product family rather than treating all batches alike.\nHelps: More meaningful quality and production monitoring.\n\n4. CAPACITY → ORDER PRIORITIZATION\n\nPain Point: With a stated capacity of up to one lakh vials per shift, the commercial question becomes which enquiries/orders should receive priority when capacity is constrained.\nSaivyy: Combine expected volume, customer value, product complexity and available capacity → prioritize production opportunities.\nHelps: Better utilization of specialized manufacturing capacity.\n\n5. CUSTOMER → ADDITIONAL INJECTABLE OPPORTUNITY\n\nPain Point: A client manufacturing one dry injectable with Osper may have other products suitable for the same facility.\nSaivyy: Customer product portfolio → identify additional dry-powder injectable opportunities.\nHelps: Increases revenue per manufacturing relationship.\n\nBEST OPENING:\n\n“Because Osper is specifically built around sterile dry-powder injections, including beta-lactam and general categories, when a new RFQ comes in, how quickly can your team determine whether it fits your exact manufacturing capability and capacity?”\n\nImported via Excel Import: Indian Pharma Expo 2022.xlsx — Assigned to Vidushi singh",
